# Classes — the unit of code

## A blueprint of state + behaviour

A class bundles what a thing **knows** (fields) with what it **does** (methods):

```java
public class BankAccount {
    long balance;                 // state
    void deposit(long amount) {   // behaviour
        balance = balance + amount;
    }
}
```

## Class vs object — cutter vs cookies

```java
BankAccount a = new BankAccount();
BankAccount b = new BankAccount();
a.deposit(100);   // a.balance = 100, b.balance = 0
```

One class, many objects — each with its **own** state.

## `this` — the object itself

```java
void setBalance(long balance) {
    this.balance = balance;   // field ← parameter
}
```

**Model the domain:** name concepts (`Order`, `Customer`), give each small responsibilities.
